# Agent-legible website (markdown twins, llms files, content negotiation)

Canonical: `rules/agent-legible-website.md`

1. Prove every route in the real build; `_`-prefixed App Router folders never route, and unit tests importing `GET` cannot catch it.
2. Every fact a human sees, including client-state-only content, is in the markdown twin or llms files.
3. Agent-surface caches clear on the same event as the human page; never cache non-200, redirects or maintenance pages.
4. `Vary: Accept` on negotiable URLs; parse q-values; prefer `.md` URLs for shared caches.
5. Convert content, not controls, with a real HTML parser; keep consent, legal text, step numbers, FAQs, tables.
6. Add footer disclaimers to every twin header.
7. Twins: not in sitemap, `X-Robots-Tag: noindex`, `Link rel=canonical`.
8. Backend errors return 503, never 404 or an empty 200.
9. Self-fetch via `127.0.0.1`, no redirect following, timeout, de-duplicated misses.
10. Read-only agent surface; in regulated products a person accepts terms and starts the trial.
